          "Founder identified that the Coverage Made To Last rendering again failed the governing visual controls: the fleet interiors were not visible, the initial school buses ignored the current 22nd-century school-bus control, and the outputs were infographic/poster boards rather than the controlled photorealistic/cinematic rendering language. The Founder also had to demand the Mirror Review even though the first failed rendering should have triggered it automatically.",
          "Failure mechanism: I did not execute ML-013/014/015/018/019/020 as an actual pre-tool and pre-presentation gate. The first generation used an infographic/poster format, showed fleet exteriors only, and rendered ordinary school buses. After the Founder corrected the school buses, the retry changed the exterior treatment but still presented a poster/infographic and still omitted fleet interiors. I treated labels and exterior appearance as sufficient even though the Fleet Interior Cross-Ref controls the inside of the vehicles and the Founder-established rendering expectation requires the fleet interior to be visually shown. This was a known same-class visual failure and should have been stopped before presentation.",
          "Immediate correction: the visual-rendering failure class remains quarantined under ML-019 until one compliant re-entry rendering passes preflight. Preflight for Coverage Made To Last is locked to exactly 12 vehicles: 3 Mega Buses (ADA/Mixed/Non-ADA) for outreach, education, resources, exhibitions and regional travel; 3 Double-Deckers as mobile roofing workshops with no mobility split invented; 3 Tour Buses (ADA/Non-ADA/Mixed) for statewide travel, education, resources, community outreach and exhibitions; 3 22nd-century School Buses for supplies with no mobility split invented. A compliant fleet rendering must physically show BOTH exterior and interior views for each vehicle family, with accessibility distinctions visibly represented where assigned; interiors must inherit mission-specific controls and cannot be replaced by captions. The visual form must be photorealistic/cinematic, not an infographic, poster, schematic or presentation board.",
          "Open proof requirement: before presenting the next Coverage Made To Last rendering, confirm exact 12-vehicle checksum, assigned mobility only where Founder specified, 22nd-century school-bus body control, supply-purpose interior for school buses, mobile-roofing-workshop interior for Double-Deckers, outreach/education/resources/exhibition interiors for Mega and Tour buses, stable Wi-Fi/renewable/durable/restroom/accessibility requirements where applicable, and visible interior/exterior depiction. The institution itself remains developing / not saved / not approved unless separately Founder-directed.",
