          "Pre-Render Mirror Review — Safely and Humanly Cleaning The Space Legacy Extermination",
          "2026-09-15",
          "PRE-RENDER REVIEW — HOLDS WITH REQUIRED HUMANE/SAFETY BOUNDARIES",
          "Founder directed a Mirror Review before rendering and then supplied the developing design for Safely and Humanly Cleaning The Space Legacy Extermination.",
          "Cross-reference passed for prompt fidelity, inherited physical controls, Chrys' Steward Common Area, palette, natural light/bay windows, 10 quiet pods, and the exact 12-vehicle fleet. Second-pass review surfaced additional inherited controls that must be visible in the rendering: the Legacy-wide Steward Common Area minimum (at least 2 shower stalls, full kitchen, convertible table-game equipment, quiet/decompression space), the Founder-directed 22nd-century school-bus visual control where school buses exist, and the Fleet Interior Standard for future fleets. A substantive control conflict was also identified: the Founder-wide Humane Participation Full-Stop prohibits labeling pain/stress/fear as humane for animals, while some proposed thermal, cryogenic, controlled-atmosphere and lethal pest-treatment concepts could cause distress or death. Hazardous-gas/cryogenic/chemical spaces require licensed engineering, ventilation, detection, interlocks, decontamination and restricted-access controls.",
